# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

Each resource manages one autoscaler policy for a specific cluster region and cluster type (`PRIMARY` or `READ_REPLICA`). Create a separate resource for each region (and read replica) that should have its own policy.

!> **Warning:** When `status = "ACTIVE"`, set `ignore_num_nodes_changes = true` on the matching `ybm_cluster` `cluster_region_info` region. This prevents autoscaler-driven `num_nodes` changes from being treated as Terraform drift. Explicit `num_nodes` changes made in the Terraform configuration are still applied. See the [ybm_cluster](cluster.md) `ignore_num_nodes_changes` attribute and the autoscaler-drift-handling example.

~> **Note:** When resizing a region to a `num_nodes` value outside the currently active autoscaling policy `[min, max]`, update and apply the autoscaling policy before resizing the cluster.

Use two applies:

1. Update the `ybm_autoscaler_policy` `min`/`max` and run `terraform apply`.
2. Update `ybm_cluster.cluster_region_info[].num_nodes` and run `terraform apply` again.

